From 89bbe60ab127cf71d238856a19c1e74b16bc36bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dre Gilley <dre@dregilley.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:06:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] WIP: G70 deadzone also when the torque tune is re-run;
 more D2C4 tests

sunnypilot re-runs configure_torque_tune through the interface instance when
NNLC or EnforceTorqueControl is on, without a deadzone argument, which reset
the G70 2024 deadzone to 0 while the curvature low-pass stayed. The Hyundai
interface now defaults the deadzone from its per-car table (other Hyundai cars
keep 0.0; generic code unchanged).

Tests: deadzone survives the re-run; filter vs reference recursion across
inactive/active with changing input and reset(); filtered request reaches
jerk, feedforward and the extension; deadzone edges at two speeds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
